NEARS-1710 delta re-QA (cycle 5) — route-scoping proof, DeliveryApp on emulator-5572
HEAD 2780cabd. App-side AppLogger [NET] lines (debug console), QA proxy in front of
the local Laravel dev server serves the two HTML endpoints under test control.

--- Case A: Terms fetch in flight (20s), user navigates to Privacy ---
proxy served:  /api/v1/terms-and-conditions   (t0)
proxy served:  /api/v1/privacy-policy         (t0+3s)   <- Privacy fetch WAS issued (not dropped)
app: [NET] GET endpoint=/api/v1/terms-and-conditions
app: [NET] GET endpoint=/api/v1/privacy-policy
app: [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/privacy-policy http_status=200
app: [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/terms-and-conditions http_status=200   <- LATE Terms response ARRIVED
screen after the late Terms 200 landed:
  label="Privacy Policy"            (app-bar title)
  label="NEARSQA-PRIVACY-MARKER"    (body still Privacy — late Terms payload discarded)

--- Case B: reverse order, Privacy fetch in flight (20s), user navigates to Terms ---
proxy served:  /api/v1/privacy-policy         (t0)
proxy served:  /api/v1/terms-and-conditions   (t0+3s)
app: [NET] GET endpoint=/api/v1/privacy-policy
app: [NET] GET endpoint=/api/v1/terms-and-conditions
app: [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/terms-and-conditions http_status=200
app: [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/privacy-policy http_status=200         <- LATE Privacy response ARRIVED
screen after the late Privacy 200 landed:
  label="Terms & Condition"
  label="NEARSQA-TERMS-MARKER"      (body still Terms — late Privacy payload discarded)

Positive control: in BOTH cases the superseded route's response is logged as ARRIVING
(http_status=200) in the app. The screen was therefore proven to DISCARD a delivered
payload, not merely to never receive one.

--- Re-entrancy guard, non-vacuous exercise ---
Same route re-entered twice while a 15s fetch was in flight (two full screen entries,
two getHtmlText calls): proxy logged exactly 1 request; content still landed.
3 rapid taps on Retry (~150ms apart, 8s response delay): proxy logged exactly 1 request.

--- Full-session failure sweep ---
3 x [FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/terms-and-conditions http_status=500 type=ApiFailure
          msg="unhandled api response"
  -> all three are the deliberately forced 500s used to reach the error state; each is
     paired with the visible error card (no silent failure path).
0 unhandled exceptions, 0 EXCEPTION CAUGHT, 0 RenderFlex overflows.
